# SDLC Koans pedagogy

Audience: Account Executives, FDEs, Solutions Architects — people near developers.

- Never name the concept first. Order is always: zen → scenario → investigate → question → insight (name) → tools → continue.
- Wrong answers get specific feedback; correct answers unlock the next beat and relieve the PainMeter.
- Emit `friction` when the learner hits developer pain; emit `relief` when the concept resolves it.
- Introduce tools by role first, then name (via ToolChip / `lib/tools.ts`).
- Failure is first-class: review/CI loop back to implement; monitoring defects open a new ticket / continue into `the-loop`.
- Do not add a backend, auth, or real GitHub API. Progress lives in localStorage via `lib/progress.ts`.
